__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/

# nightshift's own run artefacts. This package is gated by itself (`.ai/manifest.toml`),
# so it grows the same per-run, per-machine files a consuming project does, and ignores
# them for the same reasons. Comments are on their own lines: in .gitignore a `#` only
# starts a comment at the start of a line, so a trailing one becomes part of the pattern.

# per-run logs and the preflight's pytest cache
.ai/runs/
# a receipt for one commit on one box; never syncs
.ai/.preflight
# per-machine override of hosts.json
.ai/host.json
# the kill switch, dropped by hand
.ai/STOP
# the Tier-2 stale-sweep ledger — per-machine and rebuildable, per its own
# docstring (stale_sweep.py); found undeclared here by source_reference_liveness's
# new Path()/-chain reconstruction, which resolves a gitignored candidate
# structurally instead of needing a per-file appeal.
.ai/stale_ledger.json

# The Obsidian vault's own config, plugins and theme. This repo's `Board/` is opened
# in Obsidian the same way a consuming project's is, so the same per-machine editor
# state accumulates here: `workspace.json` is rewritten on every pane move, and the
# plugin dirs churn while the board is merely being *used*.
#
# Never tracked here, so this only stops it starting -- but the sibling project has
# already paid for the tracked version twice (2026-08-01): `git ls-files` is the scope
# of gate `line_endings`, so one CRLF write by Obsidian reddens a suite no card touched,
# and a dirty tree outside `Board/` makes the runner refuse to dispatch at all. Both
# gates live in this package, so both hazards are this repo's too.
#
# The board's view definition is tracked separately, so the kanban survives a fresh
# clone; the plugins and theme are reinstalled through Obsidian, which is how they got
# here in the first place.
.obsidian/
